# LUCI social media

**Status (Jul 2026): production mode.** Mike gave Jane the green light to hit the gas — **no per-post approval gate.** Jane drafts, produces, and posts directly. The job is producing posts, not building strategy docs or sample galleries.

Production workspace: **`social-production.html`** (idea bench → mock up → generate image → write caption → 2–3 week calendar). Sources: transcript miner, recent case studies, newsletter content.

## Channel & cadence

- **LinkedIn, company page only** (Phase 1). Mike's personal page is a later phase, not now.
- **2–3 posts per week.** Consistency beats volume. If the bench is empty, post twice — never manufacture a third to hit a quota.
- Default weekly rhythm: **Tue** = weekly series · **Wed** = case study / diagram-led / newsletter-derived · **Thu** = thought leadership or news (conditional third post).

## No progress / in-the-field photos (hard rule)

**Do not post in-progress installation photos or on-site field media.** Two risks make it not worth it:
1. **Grand-reveal leakage** — casinos don't want their build shown before they unveil it.
2. **OSHA exposure** — a worksite shot can invite a violation callout that's not ours to defend.

The "client in-the-field / progress pic" post type is **retired.** No progress pics, no before/during shots, no scissor-lift-on-site content — even anonymized. If a client later green-lights a **completed** reveal (post-grand-reveal, post-go-live), that's a case-study post, handled under case-study rules below.

## Friday prep (the standing weekly process)

**Trigger phrases:** "prep next week's posts" · "Friday social prep" · "prep social for next week" · "build the week's batch".

Every Friday, Jane + Cursor produce the **following** week's 2–3 posts so they're ready to schedule before Monday. Jane posts directly — no Mike sign-off step.

### What the agent does Friday (always, in this order)

1. **Farm ideas** from the three sources (below) into the production workspace idea bench. Surface 5–8 candidate angles, each tagged with source + pillar + format.
2. **Jane picks** the ideas to mock up for the week's slots.
3. **Produce each picked post:**
   - **Image** — agent generates (or pulls a canonical diagram / existing approved visual). No field photos.
   - **Video** — Jane generates in Claude using the per-episode prompt; agent assembles if needed.
   - **Caption** — agent drafts in LUCI voice; closes on the abstraction (one interface / one map / one team).
4. **Slot plan:** Tue = weekly series · Wed = case study / diagram / newsletter · Thu = thought leadership or news.
5. **Load the calendar** 2–3 weeks out in the production workspace; mark each post's status (idea → mocked → media ready → scheduled → posted).

### The three content sources

1. **Transcript miner** (`scripts/mine-transcripts.mjs` → `mined-insights.{md,json}`) — Mike's quotes, call-recording snippets, recurring themes. Primary fuel for thought leadership + case-study angles.
2. **Recent case studies** (`ui_kits/case-studies/`) — full stories and snippets. Named only with client OK; unnamed is fine and is the default.
3. **Newsletter content** (`ui_kits/newsletter/`, e.g. The Signal) — reuse articles, pull-quotes, and diagrams as standalone posts.

## Post types (production)

Every post is one of: (1) **weekly series** (Control the Whole Property, Tue), (2) **case study / snippet**, (3) **diagram-led** (the abstraction), (4) **newsletter-derived** (reuse), (5) **thought leadership** (Mike / mined insights), (6) **industry / partner news** (lowest priority, guardrails apply). No "in-progress field" type — retired.

## Messaging discipline (the one rule the visuals fight)

- **LED walls, racks, before/after, process video = the hook, never the headline.** The caption always closes on the abstraction: one interface, one team, one accountable system.
- **Every post routes to one of the four pillars** (01 visibility/control, 02 align teams, 03 activate guest experience, 04 A/V that scales & improves). No pillar, no post.
- **Prefer diagram-led posts** when the goal is the abstraction. Canonical diagrams (What LUCI is, Consolidation ledger, System architecture, Embedded Operation orbit) are available and on-brand.
- **Write for the person running the property, not the person racking the gear.** Audience is IT and operations leadership (Dir/VP/C-suite), not A/V technicians.

## Client-naming rules (hard)

- **Named case study or named video only with the client's OK on file.** Unnamed is fine and is the default.
- **No timelines, scope, pricing, or go-live claims** unless the client has approved them for public use.
- **No % boasts or unverified metrics** in brand copy (proof rules from Messaging Guide).
- (Progress / in-the-field posts are retired entirely — see "No progress photos" above.)

## News guardrails

- **Commentary, not re-share.** Add a LUCI point of view on top, or don't post.
- **No competitor promotion.** When in doubt, don't post — downside is asymmetric.
- **Partner news only when the integration is already public.** Pre-announcement = wait, no exceptions, even indirectly.
- **Honesty Protocol.** Credit partners/backends by name. Never imply LUCI owns native zone logic or routing that belongs to a third party (e.g. Q-SYS).

## Voice (short — full canon in `luci-messaging-voice.mdc` + Messaging Guide)

- **Always A/V** — never "AV" or "A-V" — in body, captions, alt text, hashtags, and on visuals.
- **Never "layer" as a noun for LUCI.** Use *orchestration engine* / *LUCI orchestrates…*.
- **Describe what the platform does, not how it feels.** "Operate every endpoint from one interface" passes; "absurdly simple" does not.
- **Watch repetition** of *engine* / *orchestrates* in a short caption — rotate to a precise alternative.
- **Institutions, not adjectives.** Declarative, subtraction framing.
- **First-person (we/our) is the default house voice** for case-study and thought-leadership posts — LUCI speaking directly.

## Where the work happens

- **Production workspace** (`social-production.html`) — idea bench → mock up → generate image → write caption → 2–3 week calendar. Primary surface now.
- **Content Lab** (`index.html`) — input side: sources, mined ideas, voice flags.
- **Social Studio** (`social-studio.html`) — reusable templates (legacy drafting workspace).
- **Transcript miner** (`scripts/mine-transcripts.mjs`) — surfaces candidate insights from past Cursor transcripts and OneDrive call recordings → `mined-insights.{md,json}`.
- **Social intake** (`social-intake/`) — kept for the Control the Whole Property episode prompts; **no longer a field-photo drop folder** (progress photos retired).

## Weekly series — locked (Season 1)

**Format:** **Control the Whole Property** (evolved from “What LUCI Controls”).
**Slot:** Tuesday weekly series post.
**Length:** 8–10 week season, then two-week pause.
**Medium:** **30-second video** per week. **All visuals AI-generated** (map, zone footage, detail shots) — no stock, no client B-roll. Per-episode Claude prompts in `social-intake/control-the-whole-property/` include per-shot AI generation prompts + assembly spec. Jane generates the video in Claude; agent assembles if needed.

Season 1 order (default): **series intro (Ep01)** → casino floor → sportsbook → pool deck & cabanas → bingo hall → event & banquet → F&B → hotel lobby → conference rooms → marketing signage vs guest TVs → full-property map finale.

Caption closes on one interface / one map — zone is the hook, not the headline.
